ers and the nonvoter, whereas M-bootstrap-contract says the cluster can only be bootstrapped once from a single participating voter. M-helper-bootstrap demonstrates repository tests using repeated identical per-node bootstrap, so the discrepancy is not proof of an illegal history; however it does not resolve the public caller duty for this fixed driver. Repair only initialization by bootstrapping the elected voter and letting other empty constructor-created nodes participate through real RPC handlers; preserve membership, election, pre-replication failure policy and the oracle. NewRaft permits empty stores and requestVote explicitly handles empty peer lists, so this has a sourced route rather than inventing histories. This review does not clear correspondence pending that repair and fresh execution.\",\n    \"resolved_by\": null,\n    \"resolution_checks\": []\n  }\n]\ncapacity {\n  \"remaining\": {\n    \"agent_calls\": 33,\n    \"experiments\": 5,\n    \"audit_units\": 3,\n    \"semantic_reviews\": 5,\n    \"revisions\": 3\n  },\n  \"remaining_seconds\": 1400.083426094,\n  \"new_obligation\": true,\n  \"direct_execution\": true,\n  \"source_investigation\": true,\n  \"exhausted\": []\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
