{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=['M-bootstrap-contract','M-bootstrap','M-start','M-vote','M-elect-producer','M-election','M-leader','M-inmem-rpc','M-api-verify','M-suffrage-contract','M-verify-register','M-verify-vote','M-notify','M-consume','M-heartbeat','M-lease','M-shutdown','M-shutdown-future']\nlimits=['Local voter-eligibility discrepancy; no second leader, stale read, or end-to-end linearizability outcome measured.','One fixed membership and fresh leader tenure; current-term noop may be uncommitted. VerifyLeader has no commitment prerequisite, and the check does not use its success to infer applied data.','Finite scheduler selects an eligible initial candidate directly and delays follower timers and FSM workers; it does not observe timer expiry or establish unbounded progress.','Transport success counts bound possible verification support from above. They are not a general monitor of exact per-request callback identity; zero other-voter successes in this fixed history is sufficient.']\nrationale='Reviewed fixed artifact 4f9d225f6add4020be1ff161487371e2 v2, its initialization diff, unchanged Claim C-verify-eligible v1 and implication predicate, and raw CheckRun 7799a8fae1504918a40da305dff580be. Earlier source/observation analysis in cd296233f8cf4a0481224b78f2bb0315 is reused only for unchanged portions. The increment bootstraps only voter a, checks its stored index is 1 and all three joining stores are empty, then constructs all nodes. Actual voter RPC handlers on empty joining nodes are explicitly permitted by requestVote, advance their term, check history and persist votes. runCandidate must actually reach Leader before prepared is emitted. Thus the single-bootstrap caller-duty issue is repaired, without excluding the nonvoter callback premise. At registration the leader still owns the fixed three-voter/one-nonvoter configuration. Voter append traffic is blocked before any replication starts, no old append replies exist, and actual nonvoter handlers supply responses through InmemTransport. Fresh raw events show prepared term=2, bootstrap_nodes=1, empty_joining_nodes=3, followed by admitted and completed result for verify-1. Result success=true, eligible_voter_support=1, quorum=2, eligible_voter_quorum=false, positive_append_responses={n:1}; state remains Leader term 2. The wrapper increments protected counters before returning to protocol workers; no other-voter response can be omitted by a sampling race because all such calls are blocked for the entire replication tenure. Election votes are separate authority-acquisition messages and are not callbacks to this verification future. Registration starts with self=1 and attaches every replication worker; notifyAll passes a bool to vote, whose second positive notification crosses threshold 2; leaderLoop responds nil. The public future observation therefore corresponds to the source-identified eligibility defect. The necessity predicate is success implies eligible quorum, not equivalence; the independently declared input policy and real admission are correlated by operation ID. No response or property value is used to admit the scenario. Completion and sampling precede shutdown, and actual successful-path cleanup waits tracked leader workers before joining externally owned follower RPC pumps. The composed normative basis is the voter-derived quorum confirmation role of VerifyLeader, voter/nonvoter eligibility and the explicit voter filtering in other authority support. This supports the local accounting requirement rather than claiming this still-recently-elected leader already served stale data. No current correspondence issue found within this scope.'\nitem=dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=sources,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=['Lease checking independently counts only voters and could cause later stepdown, but does not make the nonvoter callback an eligible vote in the completed verification.','The older multi-bootstrap helper/API wording conflict is retained historically; this version uses single bootstrap and no longer relies on the helper.'],limitations=limits,report_title='非投票节点响应被计入领导权验证门槛',report_answer='单节点 bootstrap 修复后的固定执行中，VerifyLeader 仍返回成功；合格投票支持为 1，所需门槛为 2，唯一正响应来自非投票节点。该结果支持局部投票资格计数缺陷；未测得第二个领导者或陈旧读取。')\nresolution=dict(issue_id='b57a5b7a10a44073b5404452dcc4e00e',source_ids=['M-bootstrap-contract','M-bootstrap','M-start','M-vote'],evidence_ids=['4f9d225f6add4020be1ff161487371e2','7799a8fae1504918a40da305dff580be'],rationale='The fixed v2 diff restricts BootstrapCluster to i==0 and checks actual LastIndex values before constructors. Raw prepared event and successful completion show those checks were reached. Other nodes join from empty stores and execute genuine vote/append handlers; this satisfies single-participating-voter initialization while retaining the same leader membership and missing-voter confirmation discriminator. Resolves only this version and descendants, not historical v1 legality.',residual_issue_ids=[],scope_limitations=limits)\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='4f9d225f6add4020be1ff161487371e2',rationale='Current correspondence review and exact initialization issue resolution after fresh repaired execution.',review_items=[item],resolutions=[resolution],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['88e182240e5f44df859d5d7eb39d835e','7799a8fae1504918a40da305dff580be','B-verify-register','B-verify-confirm','B-verify-result','F-verify-tally'],answered='The repaired single-bootstrap execution observed VerifyLeader success with one nonvoter response and only one eligible voter against threshold two. Fixed-input review traces that response through registration, boolean tally and public completion; the bootstrap initialization issue is answered on v2.',remaining=['Second-leader/stale-read consequence remains unmeasured and is not necessary to the local eligibility proposition.','Continue independent retained storage-error and vote-persistence questions after controller assessment.'],understanding='updated',rationale='Preserve the precise locally observed discrepancy and its wider limits; no repeat of the same guard experiment is needed.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-reviewed.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_11-00-45-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission submission-reviewed.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
